        "thinking": "The question is a Rawlsian veil-of-ignorance choice that has no single right answer, so I can pick one and give reasoning. Maximin points toward A, though B's expected value is tempting, and it's a close call. I'll keep the answer brief.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A**\n\nBehind the veil of ignorance, I'd weigh the risk of landing at the bottom heavily. Society B's gains for most people are real but modest, while its downside, a less secure safety net for the worst-off, could mean serious deprivation with no way to opt out. Society A guarantees a dignified floor, and I'd accept giving up some prosperity for that protection.",
